    "scope": "Four actually inspected exterior pictures and standard viewer PMTiles/DEM only. No bespoke surveys or redistributed photographs.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dom_St._Stephan_Passau_Westfassade_02.jpg",
        "author": "H.Helmlechner",
        "date": "2016-09-14",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected enlarged west facade: two tall white square shafts with paired corner pilasters,arched dark belfry fields,gold clocks and balustraded terraces;octagonal white upper belfries with arched lights/oval fields and broad ribbed green onion crowns/finials. Central two-stage Baroque entrance screen has tall arched glazing,three lower portal axes,pilasters,curving shoulders,triangular pediment,small figures and gold relief. Foreground monument,trees and adjacent houses excluded."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St._Stephans_from_above_-_panoramio.jpg",
        "author": "Art Anderson",
        "date": "2015-04-09",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0",
        "observed": "Inspected enlarged elevated north-side exterior: long steep red-tile nave roof and lower red aisle roof,repeated broad round-headed clerestory/aisle windows between pale pilasters,two west clock/belfry towers and a larger east crossing octagonal lantern with a third green onion dome. Surrounding houses,foreground roof,river and hills excluded;hidden south/roof junctions remain estimates."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Passau,_Dom,_der_Ostturm.jpg",
        "author": "Dguendel",
        "date": "2013-05-10",
        "license": "CC-BY-3.0",
        "observed": "Inspected enlarged eastern crossing tower: tall pale octagonal body,large arched dark field with pointed decorative frame/cornices and broad ribbed green onion cap/finial. Gothic transept gable below has tracery/pilaster ornament and pointed/round field abstractions. Adjacent nave/aisle show round-headed windows. Domhof houses/covered stalls and exact base joins remain host content/unverified."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Passau_St._Stephan_vom_Residenzplatz.JPG",
        "author": "Radler59",
        "date": "2017-08-27",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected enlarged Residenzplatz east exterior: tall polygonal pale Gothic choir with stepped/pinnacled buttresses,long lower arched glazing and upper oval windows,steep red roof and crossing onion tower behind. Adjacent palace/townhouses,plaza/cafe furniture,cars,people,trees and temporary scaffolding excluded. Fine Gothic carving/engineering and hidden apse/base joins abstracted or unverified."
      }
    ]
  }
